          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em volume conjectures
            are a class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjectures"} conjectures
            (slightly differing in generality and assumptions), saying that on a suitable (in particular:
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+3-manifold"} hyperbolic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-manifold"} 3-manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} large N limit
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%28n%29"} SU(n)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+observables"} quantum observables
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            \-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colored+Jones+polynomials"} colored Jones polynomials
            or more generally
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RT-invariants"} RT-invariants
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TV-invariants"} TV-invariants
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equal
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+volume"} complex volume
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            For a few special cases of 3-manifolds there are explicit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proofs"} proofs
            of the volume conjecture(s). Besides this there is an abundance of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computer+experiment"} numerical evidence
            for the volume conjectures, using computer algebra such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SnapPy"} SnapPy
            (see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Zickert07"} Zickert 07
          %p
            Hence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experimental+mathematics"} experimental mathematics
            strongly suggests that the volume conjectures are true. But a conceptual explanation (let alone
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            has remained open (
            %a{:href => "#Witten14"}> Witten 14, bottom of p. 4
            ).
          %p
            But an explanation via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+duality"} AdS/CFT duality
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d%2F3d+correspondence"} 3d/3d correspondence
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapped
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GangKimLee14"} Gang-Kim-Lee 14, 3.2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GangKim18"} Gang-Kim 18 (21)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AsAdSCFTPlus3d3dDuality"} below
          %h3#for__on_knot_complements
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
            on knot complements
          %p
            The original
            %em volume conjecture
            (also “Kashaev’s conjecture”, due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kashaev95"} Kashaev 95
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colored+Jones+polynomial"} colored Jones polynomial
            by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#MurakamiMurakami01"} Murakami-Murakami 01
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+N+limit"} large N limit
            of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colored+Jones+polynomial"} colored Jones polynomial
            (for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot"} knot
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            gives the simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
            (for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+knots"} hyperbolic knots
            this is the volume of the complementary
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+3-manifold"} hyperbolic 3-manifold
          #eq:KashaevConjecture.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo →
                      %mn ∞
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi π
                        %mi log
                      %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo ;
                      %mi q
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi π
                            %mi i
                          %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo |
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi vol
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  lim_{N \to \infty}
                  \\left(
                  \\frac{
                  2 \pi log
                  }
                  {N}
                  \\left\vert
                  V_N(K; q = e^{\frac{2 \pi i}{N}})
                  \\right\vert
                  \\right)
                  \\;=\;
                  vol(K).
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo ;
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_N(K; q)
            is the ratio of the values of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colored+Jones+polynomial"} colored Jones polynomial
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unknot"} unknot
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo ;
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo ;
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ◯
                      %mo ;
                      %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  V_N(K; q) = \frac{J_N(K; q)}{J_N(\bigcirc; q)}.
          %p
            The simplicial volume of a knot complement can be found via its unique
            %strong torus
            decomposition into hyperbolic pieces and Seifert fibered pieces by a system of tori. The simplicial volume is then the sum of the hyperbolic volumes of the hyperbolic pieces of the decomposition.
          %p
            If one omits the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
            in
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:KashaevConjecture"} (1)
            then the volume conjecture instead involves the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+volume"} complex volume
            (
            %a{:href => "#MMOTY02"}> MMOTY 02, Conjecture 1.2
            ).
          %h3#IdeaGenerally
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
            on general 3-manifolds
          %p
            More generally, volume conjectures state
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+of+a+sequence"} convergence
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Turaev-Viro+invariants"} Turaev-Viro invariants
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+invariants"} Reshetikhin-Turaev invariants
            on general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+3-manifolds"} hyperbolic 3-manifolds
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+volume"} complex volume
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#ChenYang15"}> Chen-Yang 15
            )
          %h3#for_
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(n)
          %p
            Generalization from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%28n%29"} SU(n)
            %a{:href => "#ChenLiuZhu15"} Chen-Liu-Zhu 15
          %h2#proof_strategies Proof strategies
          %h3#AsAdSCFTPlus3d3dDuality As combined AdS/CFT + 3d/3d duality for wrapped M5-branes
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GangKimLee14b"} Gang-Kim-Lee 14b, 3.2
            %a{:href => "#GangKim18"} Gang-Kim 18 (21)
            it is argued that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+conjecture"} volume conjecture
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+3-manifolds"} hyperbolic 3-manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^3
            is the combined statement of two
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualities+in+string+theory"} dualities in string theory
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+duality"} AdS/CFT duality
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d-3d+correspondence"} 3d-3d correspondence
          %p
            for the situation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapped on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^3
            (
            %a{:href => "3d-3d+correspondence#DGKV10"}> DGKV 10
            ):
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/VolumeConjectureAsAdSCFTPlus3d3dDuality.jpg", :width => "660"}/
          %p
            For review of the literature see also
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Dimofte16"} Dimofte 16, Section 4.1
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+manifold"} hyperbolic manifold
            %li
              %p
